{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "sectional-anatomy",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy",
    "order": 11
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "thorax",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy: Thorax",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "The Thorax \u2014 Two Challenges, and How We Image It",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Thoracic planning is defined by "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "respiratory motion",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "tissue heterogeneity",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (the beam crosses low-density lung, so the plan must apply density correction). The thorax is read on "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "two windows",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ": a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "lung window",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " for parenchyma and airways, and a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "mediastinal window",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " for vessels, nodes, and the heart."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Boundaries and levels orient you: the thoracic inlet superiorly, the "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "sternal angle / carina at ~T4\u2013T5",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", and the diaphragm inferiorly (moving with respiration)."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Normal Lung Anatomy in 3D",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Rotate this normal-lung model to appreciate the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "lobar anatomy",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and the branching "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "airways",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 the trachea dividing at the carina into main bronchi, then lobar and segmental branches."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Interactive normal lungs and airways. Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom. Note the asymmetry: three lobes on the right, two on the left."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "3D model: \"Lungs - normal study\" by valchanov (sketchfab.com/valchanov), CC-BY-4.0."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "t_p2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The trachea bifurcates into the main bronchi at the carina, at approximately which level?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "C6\u2013C7",
              "T4\u2013T5",
              "T10\u2013T11"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The carina sits at about T4\u2013T5, near the sternal angle \u2014 a stable midline landmark for localization and setup checks."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "A Lung Carcinoma in 3D",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This model shows a "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "lung carcinoma",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " in relation to the surrounding lung \u2014 the kind of gross tumor volume a therapist localizes on the planning scan."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Interactive lung carcinoma model. Consider how the tumor's position (central vs. peripheral, upper vs. lower lobe) changes its motion and its proximity to the mediastinal critical structures."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "3D model: \"Lung carcinoma\" by valchanov (sketchfab.com/valchanov), CC-BY-4.0."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "t_p3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Compared with an upper-lobe tumor, a lower-lobe tumor generally requires:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "A larger internal target volume, because it moves more with the diaphragm",
              "No motion management, because lower lobes are fixed"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Lower-lobe tumors sit near the diaphragm and move more with respiration, so their ITV (from 4D-CT) is typically larger than an upper-lobe tumor's."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Mediastinal Structures and Nodes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On the mediastinal window you must confidently name the great vessels \u2014 "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "ascending",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "descending aorta",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "aortic arch",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "superior vena cava",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "azygos vein",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " arching over the right main bronchus \u2014 plus the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "esophagus",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " posteriorly and the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "spinal cord",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " in the canal."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Thoracic nodal stations (e.g., paratracheal, subcarinal, hilar) guide elective volumes and are described relative to these mediastinal landmarks. Explore them in the workbook's "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "3D lymphatics model"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "t_p4_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which vessel arches over the right main bronchus to drain into the superior vena cava?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Descending aorta",
              "Azygos vein",
              "Ascending aorta"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The azygos vein arches over the right main bronchus to join the SVC \u2014 a classic mediastinal landmark."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Anatomic Verification in a Moving Chest",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Thoracic verification is dominated by "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "respiratory motion",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", so bony matching alone is insufficient for a target that slides with breathing."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Setup verified with "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "CBCT",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": ": match first to the vertebrae/carina, then assess the "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "tumor",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " against the ITV."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Motion managed with "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "4D-CT-derived ITVs",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": ", "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "breath-hold",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": ", or "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "gating",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "A pure bony match can leave a mobile tumor outside the high-dose region even when the spine lines up perfectly."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "t_p5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why can a perfect vertebral bony match still leave a lower-lobe lung tumor mispositioned?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "The tumor moves with respiration independently of the spine",
              "Vertebrae are never visible on CBCT"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Lung tumors move with breathing relative to the skeleton, so the target must be verified against the ITV, not inferred from bone alone."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've explored normal lung and airway anatomy, a lung carcinoma, and thoracic nodal anatomy in 3D, connected them to dual-window mediastinal reading and the carina landmark, and seen why respiratory motion makes thoracic verification a target-based task."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Cross-reference: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Thorax Treatment Planning"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
